    "plain_text": "Investment manager Michael Resnick built Tallwoods around investing its principals' money alongside client capital. The firm backs investment managers through fund commitments and direct deals, including providing initial capital to launch alternative investment strategies. Its portfolio work combines investment selection with attention to tax costs, liquidity and overlapping risks.\n\nHe also co-founded UnbundleX, a venture developing ways to separate the attributes of listed shares for trading. The proposed marketplace would let investors choose particular components of a company's risk and return, rather than buying the entire exposure. Resnick serves as a director alongside founders with backgrounds in technology, corporate finance and financial research.",
